{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_the_different_skeptical_evaluator_findings", "label": "U-0001: Skeptical Evaluator Could Not Name the Differentiator From the UI Stills", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/memory/feedback/U-0001-skeptical-evaluator-could-not-name-the-different.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TRIGGERS: designing the viewer, writing viewer copy, adding a state to the viewer. A fresh evaluator given only screenshots said 'The differentiator? I cannot tell.' The one claim that makes this evidence rather than a dashboard, 'server not contacted', rendered as 11px monospace in a grey box in a state the user must trigger. Governs viewer/index.html and ui-prototype/index.html."}, {"id": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_the_different_copy_must_be_derived_from_data", "label": "Lesson: Viewer Copy Must Be Derived From Data, Never Hardcoded", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/memory/feedback/U-0001-skeptical-evaluator-could-not-name-the-different.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In this product every line of copy must be derived from export.json, never hardcoded, because a tool whose thesis is honesty cannot contradict itself on screen. This is the root cause of all three on-screen contradictions the evaluator found."}, {"id": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_the_different_three_on_screen_contradictions", "label": "Three On-Screen Contradictions From Hardcoded Copy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/memory/feedback/U-0001-skeptical-evaluator-could-not-name-the-different.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "(1) The partial state showed a fully populated Context B card while its headline said no other context had requested the secret. (2) The error state asserted a sighting it said it could not read. (3) The scope paragraph was byte-identical across all states."}, {"id": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_the_different_context_diff_recommendation", "label": "Recommendation: Replace the Sequence Figure With a Context Diff", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/memory/feedback/U-0001-skeptical-evaluator-could-not-name-the-different.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Emphasise fields that differ and mute fields that match. Simpler than the sequence figure and fixes the 320/390 illegibility at the same time."}, {"id": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_the_different_not_reproduced_marker_colour_finding", "label": "Not Reproduced: Marker Renders Light Pink in Some States", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/memory/feedback/U-0001-skeptical-evaluator-could-not-name-the-different.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recorded explicitly as NOT reproduced: computed styles for the marker are identical across all four states. Kept in the record so a later reader does not chase it again."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_the_different_skeptical_evaluator_findings", "target": "architecture_canary_maze", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/memory/feedback/U-0001-skeptical-evaluator-could-not-name-the-different.md", "source_location": "evidence: ARCHITECTURE.md#Decisions", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_the_different_skeptical_evaluator_findings", "target": "docs_memory_feedback_u_0001_skeptical_evaluator_could_not_name_th